begin  again with heavy hearts yet another mass  shooting this time at a medical building  in tulsa oklahoma police say four people  were killed and the shooter died by  suicide they have not identified the  suspect or his motive this makes at  least 20 mass shootings since the  massacre in uvalde last week that's 20  mass shootings since last week in each  shooting at least four people were shot  or killed reagan led better from our  tulsa affiliate kotv is following this  latest attack reagan good morning we  understand that there was at least two  guns involved  good morning nate that's right police  said the killer was armed with a rifle  and a handgun it was anywhere from 35 to  40 years old now what prompted this  shooting remains unclear but a tulsa  police captain called the medical  complex where this all unfolded a  catastrophic scene  it began authorities say just after 4 50  p.m when several people called to report  an active shooter at the saint francis  medical system's natalie building in  tulsa  around four minutes later law  enforcement swarmed the facility  on the ground and just after 5 p.m  police say they were directed to the  building's second floor where they heard  those shots tulsa police captain richard  muellenberg  as they were breaching that door to the  second floor of this building the  shooting suddenly stopped we have  four civilians that are  dead we have one shooter that is dead  and  right now we believe that is  self-inflicted police recovered a rifle  and handgun and said both have been  fired  but they could not confirm whether the  shooter was targeting a specific person  had to hide in the closet  and make sure that we were safe dominica  smith is a patient service  representative for saint francis she  says she was leaving her office in the  natalie building when security told her  to lock down and take cover  just fear  with all this shooting going on i've  seen it on tv this last couple of weeks  and it's just  startling t